`format_text` uppercases and splits `"bold light red on cyan"` into `["BOLD", "LIGHT", "RED", "ON", "CYAN"]`. In the background section, it pops `"CYAN"` first to build `bg_color`, so the remaining last token is `"ON"`; therefore the `if tokens[-1] == 'LIGHT':` check for the background modifier is false, and that block is not reached. After popping `"ON"`, the foreground section pops `"RED"` first, leaving `["BOLD", "LIGHT"]`; now `tokens[-1] == 'LIGHT'` is true, so the foreground LIGHT-modifier block does run.

## Answer
{"block_at_line_50":"no","block_at_line_64":"yes"}
